<title>USA: Illinois corn harvest virtually completed.</title>
<headline>Illinois corn harvest virtually completed.</headline>
<dateline>SPRINGFIELD 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Illinois harvest was virtually completed during the week ended December 1, according to the state's Agricultural Statistics Service.</p>
<p>Corn was 97 percent harvested versus 100 percent a year ago and the five-year average of 96 percent.</p>
<p>Sorghum harvest stood at 96 percent complete versus 100 a year ago and the 98 average, the report said.</p>
<p>The winter wheat crop was rated 78 percent good to excellent, 19 percent fair and three percent poor.</p>
<p>Topsoil moisture was rated 32 percent surplus, 52 adequate, 15 percent short and one percent very short.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8720--</p>
</text>
